WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.556
[rock music playing]

00:43.043 --> 00:44.336
[breathing heavily]

00:44.420 --> 00:45.421
Eui-ju!

00:45.504 --> 00:46.839
CHAPTER 26:
YOU'RE AN OUTLIER

00:46.922 --> 00:49.008
Damn it! [grunts]

00:51.260 --> 00:52.470
[Eui-ju groaning]

00:54.889 --> 00:56.307
[doctor] Hi there. How are you doing?

00:57.141 --> 00:59.185
-[nurse] Who's the patient's guardian?
-Yes, that's me.

00:59.268 --> 01:01.520
And how long has the patient
been sweating?

01:01.604 --> 01:02.605
About 30 minutes.

01:02.688 --> 01:04.190
Does the patient have a history
of stomach pain?

01:04.273 --> 01:06.984
-I'm sorry. I don't know.
-Okay, you don't know.

01:07.067 --> 01:09.195
Please go ahead
and wait in the waiting room.

01:09.278 --> 01:10.279
Well, is it serious?

01:10.362 --> 01:11.572
-Please just wait out there.
-Okay.

01:11.655 --> 01:13.491
Okay, we have an emergency!

01:13.574 --> 01:15.034
Okay. Let's check your stomach.

01:15.117 --> 01:16.410
-It hurts. Yeah.
-It hurts?

01:16.494 --> 01:18.162
-Let me press here this time.
-It really hurts.

01:18.245 --> 01:19.997
Let's transfer her to the ER now.

01:20.080 --> 01:21.457
We're transferring her to the ER.

01:21.540 --> 01:23.000
EMERGENCY ROOM
ENTRY RESTRICTIONS

01:23.083 --> 01:24.293
We're moving her now.

01:24.376 --> 01:26.587
[tense music playing]

01:36.138 --> 01:37.181
[breathes heavily]

01:43.145 --> 01:46.524
Oh, boy. If they're taking her there,
it's one of two things.

01:47.149 --> 01:48.400
This is not good.

01:49.068 --> 01:50.194
Not good at all.

01:50.277 --> 01:51.487
[clicks tongue]

01:51.570 --> 01:52.571
It's not good?

01:53.072 --> 01:55.032
HANA UNIVERSITY MEDICAL CENTER

01:55.115 --> 01:56.909
She's going to be okay, right?

02:07.336 --> 02:08.337
Well…

02:24.812 --> 02:26.480
[nurse] Is Yeo Eui-ju's guardian here?

02:27.439 --> 02:28.607
Yes, here.

02:40.619 --> 02:41.620
Mr. Ga.

02:42.663 --> 02:44.665
Mr. Ga, what do I do?

02:44.748 --> 02:48.502
[sobbing] I knew something was off.

02:48.586 --> 02:50.963
I haven't had an appetite,
and my stomach's been acting up.

02:52.172 --> 02:54.425
I saw this on TV recently.

02:54.508 --> 02:55.593
Acute leukemia.

02:56.552 --> 02:59.221
The program said that
even healthy people can get it.

02:59.805 --> 03:03.559
And if you collapse out of nowhere,
it means it's already late-stage.

03:04.560 --> 03:05.477
I'm only…

03:05.561 --> 03:08.522
[sobbing] I'm only 18 years old.

03:08.606 --> 03:13.485
I was gonna start
buying R-rated novels myself,

03:13.569 --> 03:17.239
load up like $70 in credits
and just binge.

03:17.323 --> 03:18.657
[sobbing continues]

03:19.241 --> 03:21.452
-Mr. Ga.
-[Woo-su sighs]

03:21.952 --> 03:22.953
I…

03:25.205 --> 03:26.874
I don't have a good feeling about this.

03:27.499 --> 03:29.043
I-I think that I…

03:29.126 --> 03:31.253
[doctor] How are you feeling?

03:33.213 --> 03:34.340
What's wrong with her, Doctor?

03:34.423 --> 03:35.883
-Doctor.
-Okay.

03:37.217 --> 03:39.219
Now, please take a look
at this scan, dear.

03:39.929 --> 03:43.849
Okay. This right here indicates that
it was progressing for quite a while.

03:43.933 --> 03:46.560
Your condition was very, very poor.

03:46.644 --> 03:49.688
-You should've come in a lot sooner.
-[whimpers]

03:49.772 --> 03:52.566
Mr. Ga, what do I do?
I don't know what to do…

03:52.650 --> 03:53.692
[sighs]

03:53.776 --> 03:55.611
It's okay. I'm sure it's nothing serious.

03:55.694 --> 03:58.364
Mr. Ga. I don't want to die.

03:58.447 --> 04:00.282
-It's all right. Don't cry, okay?
-What do I do?

04:00.366 --> 04:02.284
-You're gonna be okay.
-Please call my mom for me.

04:02.368 --> 04:04.411
[Woo-su] If you get treated,
you'll be fine!

04:06.246 --> 04:09.416
My mom, I want to see my mom.

04:10.250 --> 04:11.669
Is it really serious?

04:12.252 --> 04:13.337
It's constipation.

04:19.009 --> 04:20.177
Huh?

04:22.221 --> 04:23.681
[stammering] I don't understand.

04:24.348 --> 04:27.434
Can someone be constipated enough
to pass out?

04:27.518 --> 04:28.936
Wouldn't she need some more tests?

04:29.019 --> 04:30.729
It was completely packed inside.

04:30.813 --> 04:34.108
Everything white you see in here is stool.

04:36.485 --> 04:38.487
We gave her an enema.

04:38.570 --> 04:41.115
And this is how it looks now.

04:41.198 --> 04:43.200
All cleared up. You see?

04:45.703 --> 04:48.038
Oh. And once you get home,

04:48.122 --> 04:49.748
you should weigh yourself too.

04:51.208 --> 04:52.876
You're good to leave now.

05:04.346 --> 05:06.098
[whimpers]

05:07.808 --> 05:09.893
Mr. Ga, you can just leave without me.

05:10.477 --> 05:12.479
I can… I can go back home on my own.

05:12.563 --> 05:15.149
Please don't say anything and just leave.

05:15.232 --> 05:16.233
Please.

05:17.985 --> 05:19.486
Oh, why aren't you leaving?

05:19.570 --> 05:22.406
Hurry up and leave. Please go.

05:22.990 --> 05:23.991
Please go.

05:24.992 --> 05:26.076
I don't understand.

05:28.120 --> 05:29.163
How do you

05:30.247 --> 05:31.540
always…

05:33.959 --> 05:36.170
How do you always manage to disappoint?

05:43.594 --> 05:44.595
Goodbye.

05:57.566 --> 05:58.984
[whimpers]

05:59.068 --> 06:01.195
Should I just transfer schools?

06:01.862 --> 06:03.739
Oh. Over there.

06:03.822 --> 06:06.033
-Eui-ju!
-[groaning]

06:06.116 --> 06:07.701
-[Shin] Eui-ju! Eui-ju!
-Where is Eui-ju?

06:07.785 --> 06:09.578
-Eui-ju!
-Oh, sweetheart! Oh, Eui-ju!

06:09.661 --> 06:11.288
-My goodness, Eui-ju! Are you okay?
-I'm fine.

06:11.371 --> 06:12.748
-What is it?
-I'm okay. I'm all right.

06:12.831 --> 06:15.334
-Mom, I want to transfer.
-Transfer?

06:18.087 --> 06:20.506
EPISODE 8

06:21.924 --> 06:23.092
-Mmm.
-[sighs]

06:23.175 --> 06:26.261
I wonder what made him change his mind
about the shoot.

06:27.012 --> 06:28.639
I bet he was blackmailed.

06:28.722 --> 06:31.725
Yeah. You guys don't know
how scary the principal is.

06:31.809 --> 06:33.435
Her face changes in a second.

06:33.519 --> 06:35.270
But Woo-su isn't one to be blackmailed.

06:35.854 --> 06:36.897
-You're right.
-Right.

06:36.980 --> 06:38.273
-Yeah.
-Right.

06:39.066 --> 06:41.068
[sighs] But what could
she have on him, then?

06:41.151 --> 06:42.152
[keypad beeping]

06:42.236 --> 06:44.613
-He's here. Make sure you apologize.
-[door opens]

06:44.696 --> 06:45.989
Fine, I will.

06:49.576 --> 06:51.537
You're late. You haven't had dinner yet?

06:52.329 --> 06:53.622
[clears throat]

06:53.705 --> 06:55.749
I'll get you some rice. Get him some soup.

07:02.589 --> 07:03.757
Good job today.

07:05.050 --> 07:06.760
That's all, really?

07:06.844 --> 07:09.012
I thought you said
you had something to tell Woo-su.

07:12.349 --> 07:14.017
Sorry about earlier.

07:14.810 --> 07:16.228
What are you sorry for?

07:16.937 --> 07:18.522
I said sorry. Isn't that enough?

07:23.443 --> 07:24.820
I mean…

07:28.407 --> 07:29.408
[sighs]

07:30.576 --> 07:32.202
I'm sorry for filming you,

07:32.995 --> 07:35.164
even though I know you hate it…

07:37.207 --> 07:39.376
and also for telling you to get over it.

07:44.089 --> 07:45.299
Then that's enough.

07:45.382 --> 07:46.425
Spoon?

07:46.508 --> 07:48.677
Oh. Right. The spoon.

07:50.012 --> 07:51.388
[chuckles] How cool.

07:52.472 --> 07:54.183
[chuckles]

07:55.684 --> 07:57.060
Don't you have something to say?

07:59.146 --> 08:01.148
I won't call you a fruit bat
for the next month.

08:01.231 --> 08:02.983
How about the rest of your life?

08:03.066 --> 08:04.860
-You wish.
-You sure can, four eyes!

08:04.943 --> 08:06.153
-[grunts] You fruit bat.
-What?

08:06.236 --> 08:08.113
-What? You heard him! Fruit bat.
-[laughs]

08:08.197 --> 08:09.740
He said it. Yeah.

08:09.823 --> 08:10.824
And he said he wouldn't!

08:10.908 --> 08:12.201
I didn't promise you yet.

08:12.284 --> 08:14.536
[both laughing]

08:14.620 --> 08:15.704
I'm not eating.

08:16.622 --> 08:18.207
-This is just stupid!
-Don't eat it, then.

08:18.999 --> 08:20.709
[sobs]

08:20.792 --> 08:22.502
[sighs]

08:22.586 --> 08:25.631
I thought I was finally done
embarrassing myself.

08:27.132 --> 08:28.550
[sobbing continues]

08:38.685 --> 08:40.646
Eui-ju! Damn it.

08:40.729 --> 08:41.730
[Eui-ju] It was strong.

08:42.773 --> 08:44.024
It was warm

08:45.484 --> 08:46.485
and really cozy.

08:46.568 --> 08:49.029
[heartbeat thumping]

08:52.157 --> 08:53.492
[gasps]

08:53.575 --> 08:54.576
Oh.

08:58.997 --> 09:00.457
[groans, sniffles]

09:02.876 --> 09:03.877
[sighs]

09:28.902 --> 09:30.487
The current state of constipation.

09:32.030 --> 09:34.533
According to research
amongst high school students,

09:35.117 --> 09:38.078
and the study of respective causes,
the top three factors are:

09:38.161 --> 09:42.124
lack of exercise at 43%,
fast food at 24.6%,

09:42.207 --> 09:43.834
and irregular sleep at 16%.

09:43.917 --> 09:45.919
I believe we ended up
with yesterday's disaster

09:46.003 --> 09:48.171
because you dismissed every single one.

09:48.255 --> 09:49.965
I'll keep that in mind.

09:50.048 --> 09:51.425
And thank you for yesterday.

09:51.508 --> 09:53.593
I'm not religious or anything like that.

09:54.177 --> 09:57.306
But it felt weird, showing you mercy
when you stabbed me in the back.

10:05.689 --> 10:08.275
How constipated were you that
you had to go to the ER?

10:09.067 --> 10:10.736
That's because
you didn't drink enough water.

10:10.819 --> 10:13.071
Your poop was so hard that
it was stuck in there.

10:13.155 --> 10:14.573
[stammers] No, that's not true.

10:14.656 --> 10:15.866
[Yoon] Are you okay, Eui-ju?

10:15.949 --> 10:17.784
I heard you had to go to the ER.

10:18.869 --> 10:22.539
[sighs] I can't believe you let it stay
in there until it became that bad.

10:23.457 --> 10:25.125
-You're definitely a bit slow.
-Uh…

10:25.667 --> 10:28.378
-Ah. Good job yesterday.
-Wait, Mr. Noh.

10:30.547 --> 10:33.425
What was that yesterday?
You said you knew about it.

10:34.676 --> 10:35.802
Knew what?

10:36.636 --> 10:38.847
You said you knew all about my secret.

10:39.681 --> 10:40.724
I don't know anything.

10:42.059 --> 10:43.352
[gasps]

10:46.813 --> 10:49.483
Your face has really cleared up.
You look great now.

10:53.779 --> 10:54.780
[door closes]

10:56.615 --> 10:57.616
What the…

10:58.784 --> 11:00.285
Did I fall for his lie?

11:01.787 --> 11:04.623
So, Math didn't tell him about my novel?
At all?

11:08.210 --> 11:12.464
Hey, Eui-ju! Going to the ER
for constipation is no big deal!

11:12.547 --> 11:13.840
Don't be so embarrassed!

11:13.924 --> 11:15.509
Hey, I wish you a clean finish!

11:15.592 --> 11:16.593
Good luck, Eui-ju!

11:17.177 --> 11:18.553
Constipation is no joke!

11:18.637 --> 11:20.263
Okay, I'll stop. See you!

11:26.937 --> 11:28.230
[sobs]

11:29.606 --> 11:30.732
-Oh A-rin.
-Here.

11:30.816 --> 11:32.192
CHAPTER 27:
LIKE A CAT, LITTLE BY LITTLE

11:32.275 --> 11:34.027
-Choi Yu-mi.
-Here.

11:34.111 --> 11:35.487
-Yeo Eui-ju.
-Here.

11:36.571 --> 11:37.989
-Choi Go-ya.
-Here.

11:38.073 --> 11:39.074
Choi Ji-a.

11:50.293 --> 11:51.503
-Hong Su-min.
-Here.

11:52.129 --> 11:53.213
-Jeon Chae-won.
-Here.

11:53.296 --> 11:54.714
-Im Su-yeon.
-Here.

11:55.799 --> 11:57.092
-Jenny.
-Here.

11:58.844 --> 12:01.304
Have fun with your classes today.
Good luck.

12:01.388 --> 12:03.140
[students] Thank you.

12:03.223 --> 12:04.307
Yeo Eui-ju, outside.

12:05.725 --> 12:06.935
[door opens]

12:08.228 --> 12:10.272
[students murmuring]

12:10.355 --> 12:11.356
[sighs]

12:15.444 --> 12:16.528
Why is Choi Ji-a not here?

12:17.446 --> 12:19.114
I'm not really sure either.

12:19.197 --> 12:20.240
[sighs]

12:20.323 --> 12:22.325
When I asked about her
on my first day at this school,

12:22.409 --> 12:24.995
you were the only one who answered me.
Guess what that means.

12:26.663 --> 12:27.664
Right.

12:28.206 --> 12:30.667
I thought maybe you could help Choi Ji-a
adjust to the school,

12:30.750 --> 12:31.960
maybe help her change a little.

12:32.544 --> 12:35.338
That's the reason I talked to you
and the reason I trusted you.

12:38.967 --> 12:41.303
So take more interest
and try to help a out a little more.

12:41.887 --> 12:45.098
Imagine someone waiting for you at school,
you'll force yourself to attend.

12:45.182 --> 12:47.350
Even if you don't want to,
don't you think?

12:47.434 --> 12:48.685
[gasps]

12:48.768 --> 12:50.979
But Mr. Ga,

12:51.062 --> 12:54.274
the way I see it, it's not good
to go too fast with Ji-a.

12:54.816 --> 12:57.777
You need to be gentle

12:58.403 --> 13:02.699
and take it slow
like with a cat little by little.

13:05.577 --> 13:06.661
Then do that.

13:09.331 --> 13:10.874
-Four demerit points today.
-[gasps]

13:11.791 --> 13:13.835
Will you betray my trust again?

13:13.919 --> 13:15.003
I won't, Mr. Ga.

13:23.303 --> 13:25.639
[sighs, mumbling]

13:26.515 --> 13:27.516
[grunts]

13:28.934 --> 13:30.852
Darn Choi Ji-a.

13:32.145 --> 13:33.813
Ji-a's not here again.

13:33.897 --> 13:35.148
I know.

13:36.066 --> 13:39.152
And do you know why she's always alone?

13:40.445 --> 13:41.655
I don't know.

13:41.738 --> 13:46.117
Well, some people find it more comfortable
to be alone. Maybe she's like that.

13:46.201 --> 13:51.248
Mmm… Honestly, Ji-a is a bit scary.

13:51.331 --> 13:53.750
If I rub her the wrong way,
she might blow up.

13:54.376 --> 13:55.377
[chuckles]

13:55.460 --> 13:58.505
Nah. She's not that scary.
She's just quiet.

13:58.588 --> 14:00.757
She was in my class
in our first year of high school.

14:00.840 --> 14:04.135
Whenever there was chalk on the floor,
she would put it right back on the board.

14:04.219 --> 14:07.055
Oh, and while everyone else hated
taking out the recycled waste,

14:07.138 --> 14:09.975
she'd stay until the very end
to finish it all by herself.

14:10.058 --> 14:12.644
-Mmm…
-So then… [sharply inhales]

14:12.727 --> 14:15.355
…her actions speak louder than her words.

14:15.438 --> 14:16.856
I think that's just her style.

14:16.940 --> 14:18.066
Mm-hmm.

14:18.149 --> 14:19.150
Ji-a's here.

14:20.110 --> 14:21.111
Oh.

14:22.654 --> 14:23.655
You're here.

14:24.781 --> 14:26.157
You should've been on time.

14:27.367 --> 14:29.160
Why were you late today, Ji-a?

14:32.581 --> 14:33.582
[Jenny] Mmm…

14:46.886 --> 14:48.221
[bell rings]

14:48.305 --> 14:51.099
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

14:52.726 --> 14:54.436
-Hi.
-[students] Hello.

14:58.898 --> 15:01.026
All right, turn to page 280.

15:01.109 --> 15:02.944
[students] Okay.

15:05.530 --> 15:06.531
Oh.

15:07.240 --> 15:08.241
Everyone.

15:08.325 --> 15:12.203
We'll be holding a poetry and art
exhibition to celebrate Literature Month.

15:12.287 --> 15:14.205
Each class needs
to pick one representative.

15:14.289 --> 15:16.833
Is there anyone who wants to write a poem?

15:20.795 --> 15:22.464
Mr. Yoon! Eui-ju.

15:22.547 --> 15:23.798
She's really good at writing.

15:24.382 --> 15:25.967
Right, she always doodles in her notebook.

15:26.051 --> 15:28.011
She even won a contest last year.

15:28.553 --> 15:30.805
-[students] Ooh.
-[chuckles]

15:31.306 --> 15:35.352
Oh, really? In that case, it'll be nice
if Eui-ju can be the class representative.

15:35.435 --> 15:36.853
What do you say, Eui-ju?

15:37.604 --> 15:39.898
Sure. I'll give it a try.

15:39.981 --> 15:41.858
Mr. Yoon. Can Go-ya do the drawings?

15:41.941 --> 15:43.151
Yeah, sounds great.

15:43.735 --> 15:45.403
So, Go-ya. Can you do it?

15:46.946 --> 15:49.532
Yes. Anything I can do to help.

15:50.200 --> 15:53.119
Okay then. You both are
the representatives for Class 2.

15:53.203 --> 15:54.704
[both giggle]

15:55.538 --> 15:56.665
I'm excited.

15:56.748 --> 15:58.875
-Okay. We'll do our best.
-Okay.

15:58.958 --> 16:00.960
[giggling]

16:12.681 --> 16:14.557
Are you cleaning because of your demerits?

16:14.641 --> 16:16.601
Uh… [chuckles] Yes.

16:16.685 --> 16:20.480
I don't know when I'll get more
so I need to cross them out while I can.

16:21.856 --> 16:22.899
Did you have lunch already?

16:23.566 --> 16:24.567
Yes, did you?

16:24.651 --> 16:25.652
I did.

16:28.071 --> 16:29.072
Eui-ju.

16:29.155 --> 16:30.156
Yes?

16:36.246 --> 16:39.749
Mr. Ga knows that you weren't filming
when you were out with your phone

16:39.833 --> 16:41.334
when we first met.

16:41.418 --> 16:42.419
Really?

16:42.502 --> 16:43.753
Mmm.

16:44.337 --> 16:46.339
Then why is he always picking on me?

16:47.924 --> 16:48.925
Oh.

16:50.510 --> 16:52.512
It's because of the glasses.

16:52.595 --> 16:53.596
The glasses?

16:53.680 --> 16:55.014
[sighs]

16:55.098 --> 16:56.850
Yes. His glasses.

16:56.933 --> 16:59.728
I was the one who had them
when he couldn't find them anywhere.

17:00.311 --> 17:02.480
You were the one who had his glasses?

17:03.773 --> 17:04.774
Yes.

17:05.942 --> 17:07.235
Didn't Mr. Ga tell you?

17:07.819 --> 17:09.028
He didn't say a word about it.

17:10.071 --> 17:11.322
[Eui-ju] What the…

17:11.406 --> 17:15.076
He didn't talk crap about me
for throwing his glasses away?

17:15.160 --> 17:19.164
Anyway, he's not like that
because he has hard feelings against you.

17:19.247 --> 17:20.248
So don't get too upset.

17:20.331 --> 17:23.126
[chuckles] Okay.
Thank you so much for your concern.

17:23.793 --> 17:27.922
Oh. By the way, it's truly incredible that
you made your literary debut.

17:28.006 --> 17:29.758
Nah, it's nothing.

17:29.841 --> 17:32.552
I've just enjoyed writing poetry
since I was little.

17:32.635 --> 17:35.096
At first,
it was simply like writing a journal.

17:36.014 --> 17:39.934
The emotions that were too heavy
to keep inside, I let out in my writing.

17:41.936 --> 17:45.273
After failing the New Spring
Literary Contest so much,

17:45.356 --> 17:47.901
I got lucky one day,
and was selected by a magazine.

17:48.485 --> 17:51.279
Of course, I still kept doubting myself.

17:52.197 --> 17:53.990
Was it the correct way to write?

17:54.949 --> 17:57.160
But then, I kept writing.

17:57.243 --> 18:01.414
And then I realized
it was about putting your heart into it.

18:05.335 --> 18:07.128
Yeah. Actually,

18:07.879 --> 18:11.174
I've been sort of writing novels as well.

18:11.841 --> 18:12.884
Seriously?

18:13.760 --> 18:14.761
That's cool.

18:14.844 --> 18:15.845
Not at all.

18:15.929 --> 18:16.930
[chuckles]

18:17.889 --> 18:22.268
Sir, what should I do to be really good
at writing novels?

18:24.938 --> 18:26.147
[sighs]

18:29.776 --> 18:33.446
Every single character has to have
a voice of their own.

18:35.406 --> 18:36.699
I think that's important.

18:39.077 --> 18:43.498
Every single character has to have
a voice of their own…

18:45.458 --> 18:47.126
-Right.
-Oh.

18:47.210 --> 18:50.129
-Wow, Mr. Yoon. That's cool.
-[both chuckle]

18:51.840 --> 18:53.508
I can't wait to read your piece
for the exhibition.

18:53.591 --> 18:54.425
Ah…

19:22.328 --> 19:23.538
You went to the store?

19:25.290 --> 19:26.416
Yeah.

19:26.499 --> 19:27.959
You should've come with me.

19:28.042 --> 19:29.043
Thank you.

19:30.128 --> 19:31.129
What did you do?

19:31.838 --> 19:34.716
Huh? Ah, I had a talk with Mr. Yoon.

19:34.799 --> 19:37.427
[sighs] Hey. He's really cool, you know?

19:37.510 --> 19:40.221
Apparently, he wrote poetry
since he was in middle school.

19:40.305 --> 19:42.932
He failed a known Literary Contest
until he made a debut

19:43.016 --> 19:45.727
through a different route
unrelated to the contest.

19:46.811 --> 19:49.731
You know what? I'll write something
really good for the exhibit.

19:49.814 --> 19:52.692
That way your amazing drawings
will stand out even more.

19:52.775 --> 19:54.485
Let's show everyone
your beautiful drawings…

19:55.528 --> 19:57.405
[sighs] …and how fantastic they are.

19:57.488 --> 19:59.032
Oh, I'm nervous.

20:00.491 --> 20:01.492
[slurps]

20:02.118 --> 20:03.202
Mmm.

20:03.286 --> 20:04.913
Should I start with the title?

20:04.996 --> 20:06.706
Wait, no. [inhales sharply]

20:06.789 --> 20:10.209
CHAPTER 28: I'M GOING TO TRY
TO UNDERSTAND IRRATIONAL NUMBERS

20:13.004 --> 20:15.214
FILES FOR MR. GA
REAL FILES

20:15.298 --> 20:16.674
[sighs]

20:17.967 --> 20:19.677
[smacks lips] Right.

20:19.761 --> 20:20.720
FILES FOR MR. GA

20:20.803 --> 20:22.805
[sighs]

20:23.598 --> 20:25.934
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 5

20:27.852 --> 20:29.062
[groans]

20:35.818 --> 20:37.445
[sighs]

20:37.528 --> 20:39.238
[whimpers, groans]

20:41.032 --> 20:42.033
WOO-SUUUUUUUU

20:43.993 --> 20:45.244
[sighs] No.

20:46.079 --> 20:48.289
Just skip it. [sighs] No.

20:48.373 --> 20:49.999
[clicks tongue] I'll come back to it.

20:51.042 --> 20:52.168
No. No.

20:52.251 --> 20:53.419
REAL FILES

20:58.132 --> 20:59.467
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 5

21:01.594 --> 21:04.347
[inhales deeply] Hmm.

21:04.430 --> 21:06.349
[western music playing]

21:06.432 --> 21:07.976
JUST THEN, SOMEONE GRABBED…

21:11.396 --> 21:14.565
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 5

21:15.566 --> 21:17.026
Why aren't you coming to my house?

21:17.694 --> 21:19.195
YOON'S EYES WIDEN IN SURPRISE.
IT'S SI-ON

21:19.946 --> 21:21.072
I can't go there anymore.

21:21.155 --> 21:23.116
Actually, I won't.

21:23.199 --> 21:25.451
You can't handle Discrete Math without me!

21:25.535 --> 21:27.412
If I don't teach you,
you're just gonna fail.

21:29.163 --> 21:30.665
I'll be fine.

21:31.374 --> 21:32.375
I'll pay you.

21:35.169 --> 21:36.170
What?

21:36.254 --> 21:37.547
I know you need money.

21:38.214 --> 21:39.882
I'll pay you if you come to my house.

21:41.050 --> 21:43.469
Isn't that why
you go to Kang Tae-ha's house?

21:43.553 --> 21:44.554
No, that's not it.

21:45.138 --> 21:46.264
Yes, it is.

21:46.347 --> 21:47.974
How am I any different from that punk?

21:48.057 --> 21:49.392
Well, he just is.

21:50.727 --> 21:52.562
He's different? How so?

21:53.563 --> 21:56.482
In the end, he's still trying to buy you
with money. Isn't it the same?

21:57.734 --> 21:59.652
[Tae-ha] Since you're poor,
you'll have to compensate me

21:59.736 --> 22:01.320
with something other than money.

22:01.404 --> 22:02.530
Six thousand.

22:03.406 --> 22:05.283
I'll watch how you repay all of it.

22:07.618 --> 22:08.745
[scoffs]

22:08.828 --> 22:09.912
Fine, go ahead.

22:10.538 --> 22:12.331
Get mad while you keep your pride.

22:12.415 --> 22:14.542
You're gonna take the money anyway, right?

22:14.625 --> 22:17.253
I'm curious.
How much is your pride really worth?

22:18.671 --> 22:20.465
Why do you take it this far?

22:21.132 --> 22:23.342
Why do you have to make me feel
this miserable?

22:24.343 --> 22:25.595
Do I look that easy to you?

22:25.678 --> 22:27.889
Don't waste your time.
Just think of a number.

22:29.432 --> 22:31.768
Listen. You're going to regret it.

22:32.643 --> 22:34.520
You're definitely going to regret it.

22:34.604 --> 22:35.688
Oh, no.

22:36.272 --> 22:37.523
I'll never regret it.

22:37.607 --> 22:39.025
Not even if I die.

22:41.319 --> 22:42.779
END OF EPISODE 5

22:46.783 --> 22:47.909
[Eui-ju] "Save."

22:52.038 --> 22:53.039
[sighs]

22:53.122 --> 22:53.956
FILES FOR MR. GA

22:57.251 --> 22:58.377
[sighs]

22:59.879 --> 23:00.922
You can do this.

23:01.756 --> 23:02.757
Eui-ju.

23:03.508 --> 23:04.967
You can do it. [grunts]

23:05.510 --> 23:07.053
I couldn't stop yawning.

23:07.136 --> 23:08.554
I need to go to bed.

23:08.638 --> 23:09.764
Right after dinner.

23:10.389 --> 23:11.766
What are we having?

23:11.849 --> 23:13.893
Uh… I don't know.

23:13.976 --> 23:15.561
Something really crispy and warm.

23:15.645 --> 23:17.647
-Ah… This jerk is way too picky.
-[Da-ju] Crispy!

23:17.730 --> 23:19.107
Hey, we have some curry left.

23:19.190 --> 23:20.525
-Curry?
-Yes. We have some left.

23:20.608 --> 23:21.442
Go without me.

23:23.111 --> 23:24.904
-Where are you going?
-The library.

23:26.030 --> 23:27.240
He goes to the library a lot.

23:27.782 --> 23:29.117
Hey, don't be late for dinner!

23:31.828 --> 23:34.831
[Dong-ju] Is there anything in the library
worth reading for Woo-su, though?

23:36.249 --> 23:37.458
[door opens]

23:42.880 --> 23:44.715
[footsteps approaching]

24:06.654 --> 24:08.197
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 5

24:14.412 --> 24:15.788
[Si-on] From now on,

24:15.872 --> 24:17.748
I'm gonna be a piece of work,
just for Choi Yoon.

24:19.292 --> 24:20.334
This isn't like you.

24:20.418 --> 24:21.419
No?

24:21.502 --> 24:22.378
EPISODE 5, FOR MR. GA

24:22.461 --> 24:23.296
Then what is, huh?

24:23.379 --> 24:25.131
I know you didn't even like me.

24:25.214 --> 24:28.718
You're suddenly doing this
because I got close with Tae-ha.

24:29.385 --> 24:31.554
Is that it? Are you jealous now?

24:32.305 --> 24:33.306
Jealous?

24:34.140 --> 24:35.600
You think I'm actually jealous?

24:35.683 --> 24:36.976
[scoffs, laughs]

24:38.436 --> 24:40.438
[funky music playing]

24:40.521 --> 24:41.355
That's right, I am.

24:42.315 --> 24:45.526
The way I treated you was all an act.
I didn't want you to see my true feelings.

24:46.110 --> 24:49.030
But seeing Tae-ha by your side,
it drove me crazy.

24:49.822 --> 24:51.199
[Yoon] It's no use now.

24:52.200 --> 24:53.492
Snap out of it, Yoon!

24:54.869 --> 24:57.121
You've got no one, but me.

24:57.955 --> 24:59.165
There's no other choice.

24:59.248 --> 25:02.168
Without me, you've got nothing.
You know that!

25:09.217 --> 25:10.843
END OF EPISODE 5

25:21.312 --> 25:22.688
What is it, Mr. Ga?

25:23.731 --> 25:25.191
Do you not like it?

25:26.943 --> 25:28.236
[sighs]

25:34.909 --> 25:35.910
Huh?

25:36.744 --> 25:38.329
[sighs] What was that?

25:50.341 --> 25:52.802
I made him look like
a total obsessive guy.

25:52.885 --> 25:54.303
What is he unhappy about?

26:10.152 --> 26:13.197
Oh, boy.
There's still tape around his glasses.

26:15.366 --> 26:16.367
What is it?

26:18.369 --> 26:21.831
I'm just wondering
if you aren't going to get new glasses.

26:22.415 --> 26:23.833
I ordered a new pair already.

26:25.376 --> 26:26.627
I bet they're expensive.

26:27.169 --> 26:29.714
I know I can't pay for your new glasses.
I'm sorry.

26:30.756 --> 26:31.757
You're sorry, right?

26:32.758 --> 26:33.759
Of course.

26:35.636 --> 26:37.305
Is that your excuse for giving up on math?

26:40.016 --> 26:41.267
Yes.

26:49.650 --> 26:51.277
Write it the way you want to then.

26:53.404 --> 26:54.405
What?

26:55.239 --> 26:57.491
You can stick to your version,
instead of doing mine.

26:58.534 --> 26:59.869
Are you serious?

26:59.952 --> 27:01.871
No way. Can I really do that?

27:08.294 --> 27:09.295
[sniffles]

27:10.296 --> 27:13.049
Honestly, after you caught me
writing back then,

27:13.132 --> 27:15.051
I actually thought it was all over.

27:15.551 --> 27:17.386
I figured
I'd never be able to write again.

27:18.971 --> 27:22.808
So, why are you even
letting me keep writing it?

27:33.277 --> 27:36.280
To Pythagoras,
root two was something abnormal.

27:37.865 --> 27:38.824
Huh?

27:40.034 --> 27:41.160
That's random.

27:41.243 --> 27:44.580
In those days, only natural numbers
were thought to be computable.

27:44.663 --> 27:47.875
Anything that couldn't be expressed
as a fraction was considered irrational

27:47.958 --> 27:50.961
and to be rejected.
It was an idea that shouldn't even exist.

27:52.338 --> 27:54.340
Do you know what happened
to the Pythagoreans?

27:54.924 --> 27:58.386
In the end, a student named Hippasus,
who discovered root two,

27:58.469 --> 27:59.553
met a mysterious death.

28:00.846 --> 28:02.723
They killed him because of that?

28:05.142 --> 28:07.436
It's unclear who killed him.
It's just a rumor.

28:08.020 --> 28:11.148
Dang. I guess Pythagoras
was a really scary man.

28:15.653 --> 28:16.779
Irrational number.

28:18.781 --> 28:20.241
Irrational number, right?

28:21.575 --> 28:25.246
I believe it's worth embracing that which
isn't rational or logical for that matter.

28:25.329 --> 28:27.957
I won't fall into the same trap
as Pythagoras

28:28.040 --> 28:30.751
who rejected root two
because it didn't fit his logic.

28:33.421 --> 28:35.381
Couldn't you make it a bit simpler?

28:42.596 --> 28:44.557
I want to understand irrational numbers.

28:45.266 --> 28:47.268
[light pop music playing]

29:17.882 --> 29:20.509
[Eui-ju]
Fangirling used to be my only joy in life.

29:20.593 --> 29:22.470
-Are you okay?
-But now,

29:22.553 --> 29:24.388
every time he crosses my mind.

29:24.472 --> 29:25.473
[grunts] I get so mad!

29:25.556 --> 29:27.433
-I really don't want to think about him.
-Let's go.

29:27.516 --> 29:29.602
I'm not supposed to think about him.

29:29.685 --> 29:31.061
But he's stuck in my head.

29:31.145 --> 29:33.898
[Go-ya] You're already head over heels
for him. But you're trying to deny it.

29:33.981 --> 29:35.065
That's just typical.

29:35.149 --> 29:38.194
Your words say otherwise, but your heart
is already racing toward him.

29:38.277 --> 29:40.571
[Eui-ju] No! What? Oh, no.

29:40.654 --> 29:42.114
I can't. I shouldn't like him.

29:42.198 --> 29:43.324
I simply can't!

29:43.908 --> 29:46.577
[Go-ya] Hey.
Mr. Jung's not your crush, is he?

29:47.411 --> 29:49.121
They've gotten really close.
